      {
        "id": 117898,
        "name": "mlangsdorf",
        "username": "mlangsdorf",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c4cdca/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-13T20:39:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I generally wouldn't bother unless I had knowledge of the top card(s) of the deck and it mattered. So if you're playing Nightmist or Omnitron-X is on the table, and I'd seen my top card, then I would shuffle. But if I don't know what the top card is or I know it but the only thing that is going to happen is I'll draw it on my next turn, I likely wouldn't go through the hassle of shuffling.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:50:41.460Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
